    "notes": "Inspected all 11 portable views. Nine mapped limestone stages, four straight stairways, a flat-roof summit temple, three north openings divided by two columns, and the paired north serpent terminals identify Kukulcan. First-render errors were corrected: long sloping map parts no longer become flat beams near the summit, the projecting stairs have solid backing, and the serpent feet have complete foundation support. Near levels use real shallow panel recesses and open serpent mouths with simple eye rims. Panels, columns and sculpted profiles are picture-guided medium-fi approximations; individual stone carvings and erosion are omitted."
