    "notes": "Accepted for the specific medium-fi Temple of Kukulcan exterior and approximate full-site standard-map/DEM fit. All174 pyramid/component records remain source controls. The current map supplies nine stage levels,89 tread levels plus summit landings and a30m nominal temple top. The ordinary article gives a24m body plus6m temple and approximately91 steps per side; map resolution does not prove the archaeological step count. Mapped body width is roughly56m versus the article55.3m description; projecting stairs extend the overall footprint and are not used to rescale the body. Sloped face inset, panel count/depth, balustrades, columns, serpent profiles and exposed foundation joins remain visualization estimates. The source preview seats terrain below the occupied floor only for viewing; production uses the unchanged full DEM. Hidden earlier pyramids, chambers, Jaguar Throne and exact carved motifs are not included. Known partial-residency terrain gaps are still an engine limitation and are not approved as correct partial contact. No bespoke survey or archival research was used."
